steps.body:
`if` runs a block only when its condition is `true`. Add `else if` for more checks and `else` for everything left over. C# checks them **top to bottom** and runs only the first one that matches:

```csharp
int hp = 2;

if (hp <= 0)
{
    Console.WriteLine("Game over");
}
else if (hp < 3)
{
    Console.WriteLine("Low health!");    // this one runs
}
else
{
    Console.WriteLine("All good");
}
```

The condition must be a `bool`. Comparisons produce one: `==` (equal), `!=` (not equal), `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`. Note the double `==`: a single `=` stores a value.

