steps.body:
When you compare one value against many cases, use `switch`. The **switch statement** runs code; the **switch expression** produces a value and is usually shorter:

```csharp
int day = 6;

switch (day)
{
    case 6:
    case 7:
        Console.WriteLine("Weekend");
        break;                     // every section ends with break
    default:
        Console.WriteLine("Weekday");
        break;
}

string size = day switch           // a switch expression produces a value
{
    1 => "small",
    6 => "large",
    _ => "medium"                  // _ means "anything else"
};
Console.WriteLine(size);           // large
```

In a switch statement each section must end with `break` (or `return`): C# never falls through to the next case by accident. In a switch expression the arms are tried in order and `_` catches everything else.

