A **method** gives a name to a piece of work so you can run it whenever you need it. You declare its **return type**, its name and its **parameters** (each with a type):

```csharp
Console.WriteLine(Square(4));           // 16
Console.WriteLine(Square(Square(2)));   // 16 too: 2 becomes 4, then 16
