steps.body:
`class Slime : Enemy` means a Slime **is an** Enemy: it gets all of Enemy's members for free and can add its own. A method marked **`virtual`** may be replaced in a subclass with **`override`**:

```csharp
var slime = new Slime();
slime.TakeDamage(3);
Console.WriteLine(slime.Health);       // 7: Health and TakeDamage come from Enemy
Console.WriteLine(slime.Describe());   // Slime with 7 HP

class Enemy
{
    public int Health { get; protected set; } = 10;   // protected: Enemy and its subclasses
    public void TakeDamage(int amount) => Health -= amount;
    public virtual string Describe() => $"Enemy with {Health} HP";   // virtual: may be replaced
}

class Slime : Enemy                    // a Slime is an Enemy
{
    public override string Describe() => $"Slime with {Health} HP";
}
```

A class can inherit from only **one** base class. Inside an override, `base.Describe()` calls the parent's version.

