steps.body:
Many types just hold data. A **record** declares one in a single line, with a constructor, read-only properties, a readable `ToString` and **value equality**: two records with the same values are equal.

```csharp
var a = new Card("Ace", 11);
var b = new Card("Ace", 11);
Console.WriteLine(a);              // Card { Name = Ace, Value = 11 }
Console.WriteLine(a == b);         // True: records compare their values

var low = a with { Value = 1 };    // a copy with one property changed
Console.WriteLine(low.Value);      // 1
// a.Value = 1;                    // would not compile: record properties are init-only

record Card(string Name, int Value);
```

A record like this one is immutable: instead of changing it, you make a modified copy with `with { ... }`.

